{
  "$comment": [
    "Expected packets for the EVision V2 keyboards, worked out from the OpenRGB C++ code at commit d4798c120659ec5ba2e664a9e87bedff8d36f880, not by running plugin.js: a Python re-implementation of EVisionV2KeyboardController::Query (64-byte output report: report id 4, checksum of bytes 3..63 as uint16 little-endian at bytes 1..2, command at 3, size at 4, offset little-endian at 5..6, data from 8), ::Write (chunks of 56 bytes), ::Read, ::SetLedsDirect (colour of LED i at 3 * keyvalue_map[i] of a 3 * map_size buffer, sent with command 0x12), ::RefreshLedDirect (command 0x12, offset 18, size 1) and ::EndLedsDirect (command 0x13), with the LED tables parsed from EVisionV2KeyboardController.cpp and RGBController_EVisionV2Keyboard.cpp.",
    "Replies are synthetic: the request echoed with status byte 7 = 0, which is what Query accepts (report id, checksum bytes, command and offset must match the request). The capability data is synthetic too (magic AA 55, map size at data byte 5, macro size at data byte 6, the rest 0); the map size of the real keyboards is not known (the largest slot used by both layouts is 124).",
    "Colours: device.color(x, y) answers colours[<name>] for the LED at matrix cell (x, y)."
  ],
